      "problem": "Find $det({A}^{-1})$, if $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-6-4 \\\\  & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=-\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$",
